# Theorem 8.9: Figure 4 is complete for real-Clifford+CH circuits

Clément, *A complete equational theory for real-Clifford+CH quantum
circuits* (arXiv:2602.06644): for every number of wires `n`, the equations
of Figure 4 (in the PRO form of Remark 1, see `Syntax`) present the group of
orthogonal matrices that `n`-wire real-Clifford+CH circuits generate:
the equations are sound (Proposition 3.1), circuits with the same
semantics are equal in the theory (Theorem 8.9), and every gate is
invertible in the theory.  The values lie in `O_{2^n}(ℤ[1/√2])` (they are
products of the gate matrices, whose entries are in `ℤ[1/√2]`); Lemma 4.7
identifies the group they generate inside it.

Completeness is proved here on zero and one wire (Lemma 7.1).  On two wires
it is the back-and-forth argument of Section 7.2 (`TwoQubit`): proved from
Theorem 4.4 (imported from Hadamard-Π; `theorem_4_4`, a `sorry` standing for
`QCert.HadamardPi.theorem_4_14`) and Lemma 7.5 (`lemma_7_5`, a `sorry`).  From three wires on (Section 8: Theorem 4.10,
Lemmas 8.7 and 8.8, Appendices A.3–A.4, D and E) it is not formalized
(`completeness_ge_three`, a `sorry`).  See `README.md`.
-/
import QCert.RealCliffordCH.OneQubit
import QCert.RealCliffordCH.TwoQubit

namespace QCert.RealCliffordCH

/-- Theorem 4.4 at `N = 4`, which the paper imports from Hadamard-Π [17]:
words over `𝒢₄` with the same matrix are equal by the equations of
Figure 6.  It is Hadamard-Π's Theorem 4.14 at `n = 4`, formalized in
`QCert.HadamardPi.theorem_4_14` (`(theorem_4_14 4).complete`); it is stated
here rather than imported, so that this development builds independently
of that one. -/
theorem theorem_4_4 : ∀ u v : Word Two.G4, FreeMonoid.lift (QCert.HadamardPi.sem 4) u =
    FreeMonoid.lift (QCert.HadamardPi.sem 4) v → Derivable QCert.HadamardPi.Fig6 u v := by
  sorry

/-- Lemma 7.5 (Appendix C.2): the decoding `D` maps every equation of
Figure 6 on `𝒢₄` to an equation derivable from Figure 4.  Not formalized. -/
theorem lemma_7_5 : ∀ u v : Word Two.G4, QCert.HadamardPi.Fig6 u v →
    Derivable (theory 2) (Two.decW u) (Two.decW v) := by
  sorry

/-- Lemma 7.6 (2-qubit completeness): from Theorem 4.4, Lemma 7.4
(`Two.lemma_7_4`, proved) and Lemma 7.5. -/
theorem lemma_7_6 {w v : Circ 2} (h : S.sem 2 w = S.sem 2 v) : Derivable (theory 2) w v :=
  Two.complete_two_of theorem_4_4 lemma_7_5 h

/-- Theorem 8.9 from three wires on: Theorem 4.10, Lemmas 8.7 and 8.8
(Section 8, Appendices A.3, A.4, D and E).  Not formalized. -/
theorem completeness_ge_three (n : ℕ) (hn : 3 ≤ n) {w v : Circ n} (h : S.sem n w = S.sem n v) :
    Derivable (theory n) w v := by
  sorry

/-- Theorem 8.9 (Completeness): circuits with the same semantics are equal
in the theory. -/
theorem completeness (n : ℕ) {w v : Circ n} (h : S.sem n w = S.sem n v) :
    Derivable (theory n) w v := by
  match n, w, v, h with
  | 0, _, _, _ => exact complete_zero
  | 1, _, _, h => exact complete_one h
  | 2, _, _, h => exact lemma_7_6 h
  | n + 3, _, _, h => exact completeness_ge_three (n + 3) (by omega) h

/-- The equations of Figure 4 (with (f1)–(f4) and (g) of Remark 1) present
the group generated by the `n`-wire real-Clifford+CH circuits. -/
theorem presentation (n : ℕ) : IsSubPresentationOf (theory n) (S.gen (n := n)) where
  grouplike := grouplike n
  sound _ _ h := sound n h
  complete _ _ h := completeness n h

end QCert.RealCliffordCH
